# Tidy on the Today divider (Pane, 14 Nov 2026): only with two or more loose Today tabs to sort, as a
# group takes two. A run that leaves one tab loose, or puts every tab in a section, takes it off the
# divider at once; a second loose tab brings it back. The runs are cra://debug?tidyPlan= (a model's
# answer, as Tidy applies one); tabGroups= reads what the divider is told (TidyTabsService.visibility).
budget rss=800 stalls50=30
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
env CRA_TIDY_FAKE_MODEL=1

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=1
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=2
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=3
wait 2
cra://debug?tabGroups=start
expect-log tab groups start: +tidy=withShift$
# Two of the three grouped: one loose tab left, nothing for Tidy to group.
cra://debug?tidyPlan=Pair:0,1
wait 0.5
cra://debug?tabGroups=oneLeft
expect-log tab groups oneLeft: Pair\(open rows=2/2\) tidy=hidden$
# A new tab makes two loose ones: Tidy is back (with Shift, under eleven Today tabs).
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=4
wait 1
cra://debug?tabGroups=twoLoose
expect-log tab groups twoLoose: Pair\(open rows=2/2\) tidy=withShift$
# Both into a section of their own: every Today tab grouped, no Tidy.
cra://debug?tidyPlan=Rest:0,1
wait 0.5
cra://debug?tabGroups=allGrouped
expect-log tab groups allGrouped: (Pair|Rest)\(open rows=2/2\) (Pair|Rest)\(open rows=2/2\) tidy=hidden$
reject-log fault:
